From b1a57cfe82895c2444e55e65b558ee055425248a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:16:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ts: count the PCRs the probe reads as received

The demuxer takes a program for one with no PCR, and moves its clock to
another pid, when a block comes more than half a second after the first
timestamp seen with no PCR received on the PCR pid. The probe of the start
records that first timestamp, but the PCRs it reads were not counted: a
start time or a seek after it brings the first blocks from far on, and
where LPCM sound takes most of the packets, as in a Blu-ray stream whose
video takes few bytes, a block of sound came before the next PCR. The
program then lost its clock: every later seek by time failed and landed
by the byte position, a second late.

Count the PCRs the probe reads on a pid, as PCRHandle counts those it
reads while demuxing.
---
 modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c b/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
index e8ded01..a530542 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
+++ b/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
@@ -2086,6 +2086,15 @@ static int ProbeChunk( demux_t *p_demux, int i_program, bool b_end, ts_90khz_t *
 
             if( b_adaptfield && p_pkt->i_buffer >= 4 + 2 + 5 )
                 *pi_pcr = GetPCR( p_pkt );
+            /* A PCR the probe reads counts as one received on its pid, as
+             * PCRHandle counts them while demuxing: a start time or a seek
+             * after probing the start can bring the first blocks of another
+             * stream more than half a second past the first timestamp
+             * probed, with no PCR read since, as where LPCM sound takes most
+             * of the packets, and PCRFixHandle would take a stream that has
+             * PCRs for one with none. */
+            if( *pi_pcr != TS_90KHZ_INVALID )
+                p_pid->probed.i_pcr_count++;
 
             /* Presentation endpoints, independent of the clock endpoints:
              * even a packet carrying a PCR also has a presentation timestamp.
